hot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:38"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"25"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5291946","displayName":"Roger McQueen","shortName":"R. McQueen"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4392765","displayName":"Michael DiPietro","shortName":"M. DiPietro"},"type":"saver"}]},{"id":"401892518000001040","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Anthony-John (AJ) Greer hit Frederic Brunet","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:34"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"25"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3648015","displayName":"A.J. Greer","shortName":"A.J. Greer"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"5103647","displayName":"Frederic Brunet","shortName":"F. Brunet"},"type":"hitted"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1842","fullName":"Honda Center","address":{"city":"Anaheim","state":"CA","zipCode":"92899","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1842.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17174,"officials":[{"fullName":"Ryan Gibbons","displayName":"Ryan Gibbons","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"David Brisebois","displayName":"David Brisebois","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Gord Dwyer","displayName":"Gord Dwyer","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Schrader","displayName":"Brandon Schrader","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Elias Lindholm's big 3rd period sparks streaking Bruins' comeback for 4-2 win over Ducks","description":"— Elias Lindholm assisted on the tying goal and scored the go-ahead goal in the third period, leading the Boston Bruins past the Anaheim Ducks 4-2 on Friday night for their fourth straight victory.","story":"ANAHEIM, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3041994/elias-lindholm\">Elias Lindholm</a> assisted on the tying goal and scored the go-ahead goal in the third period, leading the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/bos/boston-bruins\">Boston Bruins</a> past the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ana/anaheim-ducks\">Anaheim Ducks</a> 4-2 on Friday night for their fourth straight victory.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114778/david-pastrnak\">David Pastrnak</a> scored a tying power-play goal and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5103647/frederic-brunet\">Frederic Brunet</a> got his first NHL goal for the Bruins, who roared back from an early two-goal deficit and improved to 6-2-0.\n\n\r\n              Less than five minutes after Pastrnak converted a give-and-go with Lindholm, the Ducks failed to mark Lindholm during a power play and allowed him to tap in a pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899949/pavel-zacha\">Pavel Zacha</a> with 11:39 to play. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080221/matthew-poitras\">Matthew Poitras</a> added another goal with 3:40 left on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5275337/james-hagens\">James Hagens</a>' second assist of the night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392765/michael-dipietro\">Michael DiPietro</a> made 25 saves in his second start of the season for the Bruins.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216858/beckett-sennecke\">Beckett Sennecke</a> got his fifth goal and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4996085/tim-washe\">Tim Washe</a> also scored for the Ducks, who have lost three straight home games while giving up 13 goals. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588165/lukas-dostal\">Lukas Dostal</a> stopped 18 shots.\n\n\r\n              Ducks captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5831/mikael-granlund\">Mikael Granlund</a> sat out with an upper-body injury, and goal-scoring winger <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080145/cutter-gauthier\">Cutter Gauthier</a> filled in by moving to center for the first time in his NHL career.\n\n\r\n              Anaheim had the best chances in the first period, and it took a lead with two goals 20 seconds apart in the final minute. After Washe's long shot went in through the legs of screening teammate <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4895214/jeff-malott\">Jeff Malott</a>, Sennecke finished a strong passing sequence with Gauthier and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4755696/nikita-nesterenko\">Nikita Nesterenko</a>.\n\n\r\n              Brunet trimmed Anaheim's lead with his first goal early in the second, connecting on a power play in the 23-year-old defenseman's sixth NHL game.\n\n\r\n              After the Ducks failed to score on a four-minute power play, Pastrnak's 423rd career goal broke a tie with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3852/brad-marchand\">Brad Marchand</a> for the fourth-most in Bruins history.\n\n\r\n              The Ducks have sold out Honda Center for the first four games of a new season for the first time since 2007, when the team was coming off its lone Stanley Cup title.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Bruins: At Los Angeles on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Ducks: At <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> on Monday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-17T04:51:26Z"}}